    "title": "LEARNING WHOM TO TRUST",
    "text": "Thursday, September 18, 2025\nVolunteer firefighter Tony Rafanelli and Agnes Filkens, who previously served on the school committee, high-five hello to first-grader Teddy Benda at Melrose School during the opener Monday of “Start with Hello Week.” The theme of the day was “Who is your trusted adult.” Photos by Andrea von Hohenleiten\nThe superintendent of schools, David Raleigh, browses his phone with kindergartener Xavier Gamble- O’Donnell. Behind them is Jamestown’s state rep, Alex Finkelman.\nSecondgrader Gracesyn Klann and kindergartener Noah Klann pose with a ladder truck from the fire department.\nStudents settle into their school day in the cafeteria for their morning assembly.\nThe captain of the police department, Angela Deneault, with fourth-grader Abigail Chapman, from left and right, and kindergarteners Zelda Parkhurst, Olivia Harris and Callan Randol.\nFourth-grader Emmie Siegler high-fives police detective Jeff Petrarca.",
